From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Davanum Srinivas <davanum@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/kube-apiserver/app/testing: raise healthz poll budget to
 120 s

The kube-apiserver app/testing StartTestServer was using time.Minute (60 s)
as the healthz poll budget.  On 32-vCPU CI runners that start many packages
in parallel, RBAC bootstrap contention can push apiserver startup past 60 s,
causing kubeapiservertesting.StartTestServerOrDie to fail with
"failed to wait for /healthz to return ok: timed out waiting for the
condition" in tests like TestStructuredAuthenticationConfig,
TestCustomResourceValidation, and others in apiserver/anonymous,
apiserver/oidc, certificates, controlplane/transformation, and
clustertrustbundles packages.

Raise the budget to 120 s to match the same fix already applied to
test/integration/framework/test_server.go (patch 0001).
---
 cmd/kube-apiserver/app/testing/testserver.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmd/kube-apiserver/app/testing/testserver.go b/cmd/kube-apiserver/app/testing/testserver.go
index 7027f792f63..199e1d8e917 100644
--- a/cmd/kube-apiserver/app/testing/testserver.go
+++ b/cmd/kube-apiserver/app/testing/testserver.go
@@ -470,7 +470,7 @@ func StartTestServer(t ktesting.TB, instanceOptions *TestServerInstanceOptions,
 		t.Logf("Waiting for /healthz to be ok...")

 		// wait until healthz endpoint returns ok
-		err = wait.Poll(100*time.Millisecond, time.Minute, func() (bool, error) {
+		err = wait.Poll(100*time.Millisecond, 120*time.Second, func() (bool, error) {
 			select {
 			case err := <-errCh:
 				return false, err
--
2.50.1

